---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import avatar from '../assets/avatar.jpg';
import DecayChart from '../components/DecayChart.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="About Ankur Singhal: an exposure scientist who combines data analytics, machine learning, and software development.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I am an exposure scientist with a background in toxicology, consumer product safety, and risk assessment. I found that the hardest part of this work is often the data, so I learned to code and build software. Today, most of my work sits at the intersection of these fields.
        </p>
        <p>
          Toxic tort cases often involve specialists in exposure, toxicology, modeling, and other disciplines. When each expert processes data independently, inconsistencies can arise, and the challenge grows when the data spans decades. I bridge those disciplines as an exposure and risk assessor who also builds the databases, pipelines, and dashboards that help complex cases run more efficiently. My knowledge of hydrogeology, toxicology, epidemiology, and fate and transport helps connect details that experts working in silos might miss. For legal teams and their experts, I can turn decades of messy data into something usable, explain what it means, and identify what may be missing.
        </p>
        <p>
          I began working with <a href="https://eheinc.com/team/ankur-singhal/" target="_blank">EH&amp;E</a> as a subcontractor to evaluate lead exposures from a lead smelter to the nearby communities in La Oroya, Peru, and later joined the firm full time. Before that, I advanced from Scientist to Managing Scientist at Exponent and then ran my own consultancy.
          Today, my work spans contamination from PCBs, 1,4-dioxane, lead, asbestos, respirable crystalline silica and multiple other chemicals in settings ranging from drinking water and air to consumer products. 
        </p>

        <h2>The question behind the work</h2>
        <p>
          Nearly every project starts with the same questions: Who was exposed, to what, and how much?
          I use sampling, exposure models, data, and visualizations to answer them—and increasingly, tools that bring the data to life, with or without AI.
        </p>
        <DecayChart />

        <h2>Outside of work</h2>
        <p>
          The title says it all: I like being outside. Almost 10 years ago, I moved to Bishop, California, in the foothills of the Sierra Nevada, to enjoy climbing, mountaineering, backpacking, hiking, and other mountain adventures. Lately, I’ve been getting more into big-wall climbing and peak bagging. I’m also a member of Inyo County Search and Rescue (InyoSAR), a volunteer organization that responds to everything from medical emergencies to technical rock, snow, and ice rescues.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also play guitar. Most of all, I love being a dad to my young son, who will probably surpass my climbing accomplishments before long.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/cv">Read the CV</a> or <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside>
        <Image src={avatar} alt="Ankur Singhal" width={544} height={544} />
        <p>How to say my name</p>
        <audio controls preload="none" src="/files/ankur-name.m4a">
          <a href="/files/ankur-name.m4a">Download the recording</a>
        </audio>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
